Plain-language summary (this section is NOT the license)
======================================================================

This summary is a courtesy explanation only. It has no legal effect.
If anything here conflicts with Part A below, Part A controls.

- You may use, study, run, and share the Dynamic Drought Module (DDM)
  for any noncommercial purpose, and you may modify it, as long as you
  release your modified version under this same license: share-alike.
- Commercial use is not permitted, full stop. This document does not
  offer a path to a commercial license; that would take a separate
  written agreement with ATNI Climate.
- Every deployment must show where its data comes from: source,
  issuer, retrieval date, and terms, for every layer the tool displays
  and for every layer a deployer adds.
- Every use must follow the Tiered Sovereign Data Framework (TSDF) for
  any sovereign, Tribal, or Indigenous data the tool touches, and must
  credit ATNI Climate, with Patrick A. Freeland as Developer.
- This tool exists in service to Tribes and Indigenous Peoples. Use of
  it must not work against Tribal sovereignty, treaty rights, or
  Indigenous data sovereignty. It can, and should, be used to help any
  community that has access to it.
- The public data the tool displays (NOAA, NASA, USGS, USDA, the
  Census Bureau, the Bureau of Indian Affairs, the National
  Interagency Fire Center, and the other sources named in README.md)
  is not owned by ATNI Climate and keeps its own terms: generally
  public domain for U.S. federal works, or the issuing source's own
  specific-use terms.

