Additional Conditions
----------------------------------------------------------------------

These Additional Conditions are conditions on every license granted
above. A use that fails any of them is a use outside your licenses,
the same as a failure of any base term above.

### 1. Share-Alike

If you distribute the software, or any Derived Work (defined below),
you must license the entire Derived Work, as a whole, under this same
license: the DDM Community License, Version 1.0, unmodified except for
the addition of your own copyright notice for your own changes. You
may not add further restrictions this license does not already carry,
and you may not distribute a Derived Work under any other license.

### 2. Attribution

Every copy or Derived Work must credit, in its user interface or in
accompanying documentation:

- ATNI Climate, The Affiliated Tribes of Northwest Indians, as the
  original licensor;
- Patrick A. Freeland as the Developer of the Dynamic Drought Module;
  and
- the project name, "Dynamic Drought Module (DDM)", and its source
  repository, https://github.com/atniclimate/dynamic-drought-module.

### 3. Data Provenance

For every dataset the software displays, and for every dataset a
deployer adds (including through deployer-provided data slots
described in this repository's documentation), the deployment must
carry, and make reasonably discoverable to a viewer, that dataset's
source and issuing organization, its retrieval date or vintage, and
its terms of use to the extent the source states them. This provenance
must travel with any redistribution of the software or of the data
itself. Stripping it is a violation of this license, even where the
underlying data would otherwise be freely redistributable on its own.

### 4. Tiered Sovereign Data Framework Adherence

Any sovereign, Tribal, or Indigenous data the software handles or
displays, or that a deployer adds to it, must be handled according to
the tiers and consent rules of the Tiered Sovereign Data Framework
(TSDF), published at
https://github.com/atniclimate/TieredSovereignDataFramework. Without
the consent the TSDF's tiers require, you may not redistribute
sovereign boundary or place data, or any other Tribal or Indigenous
data, beyond what its source and the Nation or Peoples concerned
permit. When a dataset's tier is unclear, treat it as the TSDF's most
protected tier until the concerned Nation or Peoples says otherwise.

### 5. Service to Tribes and Indigenous Peoples

This software exists in service to Tribes and Indigenous Peoples. Your
use of it must not be adverse to Tribal sovereignty, treaty rights, or
Indigenous data sovereignty. Subject to that condition, and to every
other condition in this license, the software may be used to help any
community that has access to it; this license does not limit who may
be helped.

### 6. No Commercial Use

The noncommercial limitation stated in the base terms above is
absolute. This document does not offer, and nothing in it should be
read to imply, a separate commercial license; a commercial license, if
ATNI Climate ever chooses to offer one, requires a separate written
agreement outside this document.

### 7. Public-Source Acknowledgment

The public data sources this software displays, including but not
limited to NOAA, NASA, USGS, USDA, the U.S. Census Bureau, the Bureau
of Indian Affairs, the National Interagency Fire Center, and the other
federal, state, provincial, and Tribal sources named in this
repository's README.md, are not owned or licensed by ATNI Climate and
are not relicensed by this document. They keep their own terms; see
Part B below and README.md for what this repository's documentation
states about each one.

### 8. No Endorsement

You may not use the name "ATNI", "ATNI Climate", "The Affiliated
Tribes of Northwest Indians", or the Developer's name, to imply
endorsement of a Derived Work or of any use of the software, beyond
the attribution this license requires.

### Definitions (Additional Conditions)

Commercial Use means use intended for, or directed toward, commercial
advantage or monetary compensation: selling the software or access to
it, bundling it with a paid product or service, or using it in the
operation of a for-profit business, whether or not the software itself
is sold.

Derived Work means the software with any change, addition, or removal,
or any new work that incorporates the software or a material part of
it, including a modified deployment, fork, or embed that alters the
software itself. Configuration data a deployer supplies under
Additional Condition 3 is not, by itself, a Derived Work.

======================================================================
Part B: Notices
======================================================================

This Part B is informational. It records what this repository's own
documentation, principally README.md as read on 2026-09-08, states
about the public data sources the software can display. It is not a
representation by ATNI Climate about any source's actual current
license, and it does not narrow Additional Condition 7. Verify current
terms with each issuing source before relying on this section.

United States federal sources named in README.md: NOAA (NIDIS, CPC,
NWS/WPC, SPC, NCEI, HMS), NASA (GIBS), USGS (3DEP; telemetry), USDA
(Forest Service GeoPlatform, for Wildfire Hazard Potential), the U.S.
Census Bureau (state boundaries; AIANNH), the Bureau of Indian Affairs
(AIAN-LAR reservation boundaries), the National Interagency Fire
Center (WFIGS fire perimeters), NRCS, USBR, and USACE (telemetry), and
the Energy Information Administration (power plants). Works of the
United States federal government are generally not subject to
copyright in the United States and are in the public domain
domestically; a specific federal dataset may still carry a
service-specific terms-of-use page this repository's documentation
does not itemize beyond what is stated here and in README.md.

National Drought Mitigation Center (NDMC), which publishes the U.S.
Drought Monitor with NOAA and USDA as partners: terms not itemized in
this repository's documentation beyond the source citation.

Agriculture and Agri-Food Canada: issuer of the Canadian Drought
Monitor snapshot bundled with this software on a monthly cadence. A
Canadian federal source; terms not itemized in this repository's
documentation beyond the source citation.

Government of Canada, Statistics Canada, Statistical Geomatics Centre:
issuer of the 2021 Digital Boundary File this software uses only as an
internal analysis mask for the northern minimap framing, never as
rendered boundary or jurisdictional geometry. README.md states this
dataset is licensed under the Open Government Licence, Canada,
https://open.canada.ca/en/open-government-licence-canada.

EPA (Omernik Level III and IV Ecoregions), bundled as tiles: terms not
itemized in this repository's documentation beyond the source
citation.

Natural Earth: issuer of the bundled, display-only municipal place
labels; terms not itemized in this repository's documentation beyond
the source citation.

OpenStreetMap contributors, retrieved live via Overpass for the rivers
layer: terms not itemized in this repository's documentation beyond
the source citation.

Live Tribal-geography sources (U.S. Census AIANNH; BIA AIAN-LAR):
README.md states these are fetched live at view time from the
publishing federal services, held only in browser session memory,
requested with cache: 'no-store', and never bundled or redistributed
by this repository.

Deployer-provided data (the tribal and treaty slots): README.md states
these ship as empty placeholders a deployer populates with its own
authorized data, under the deployer's own governance and Additional
Condition 4 above. They are not public sources of this repository and
carry whatever terms the deployer's own data carries.

Tribal Nations whose boundary, treaty, or place data appears through
any live source, deployer slot, or future addition: that data remains
the sovereign data of the Nation concerned, governed first by that
Nation's own terms and by the Tiered Sovereign Data Framework
(Additional Condition 4), regardless of which federal or state agency
publishes or hosts it.

